{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/603759-nyarlathotep-as-a-demon","id":603759,"title":"Nyarlathotep as a Demon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-26T05:47:50-07:00","id":603759,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Nyarlathotep as a Demon","content":"So in the Cthulhu Mythos, Nyarlathotep is a creature at the center of global conspiracies, cults, and occult lore. If I were to make him into a demon though, what Embeds, Exploits, and Cipher would be in character for him? I can see him as a Psychopomp, perhaps with a Tempter/Integrator Agenda (Integrator of the Outer Gods, even). His covers though seem a bit too monstrous to get away with. Perhaps his Cipher helps with that in some way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T08:23:52-07:00","id":603841,"title":"","content":"Man, this is fun. And actually not too difficult.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d argue that the Crawling Chaos is a Messenger Tempter. That\u2019s his role, messenger of the Outer Gods, revealing them to humanity, at least in some depictions. If we\u2019re putting the Old Ones in the role of the God-Machine then he\u2019s an Integrator too, aye, but in that case he\u2019d make a better angel.<br /> <br /> So what special powers set Nyarly apart? I mean, you\u2019d want to give him some Embeds like <b>Devil\u2019s Advocate, Heart\u2019s Desire, Sum of all Fears</b> for his role as a tempter and he probably needs <b>Huge Size</b> for his Demonic Form (the God of the Bloody Tongue isn\u2019t exactly small), but that\u2019s nothing special or difficult. What makes Nyarly mechanically tricky is the whole \u2018masks\u2019 schtick. He can be in multiple places at once, wearing a human face in one and a horrific inhuman face in another.<br /> <br /> How to model that in Demon? First off, he\u2019ll need a high Primum just to maintain a stable of multiple Covers. Next he needs powers that let him appear in multiple places at once \u2013 so, that\u2019s <b>Alibi </b>from the Embeds, <b>Terrible Avatar </b>(for sure) and maybe <b>Multiple Images</b> from the Exploits. <b>Persistent Legend</b> and <b>Associate and Integrate</b> will help to keep those Covers distinct (and powerful) and <b>Identity Theft</b> adds more options to his bag of masks.<br /> <br /> Our next problem is that while some masks appear as ordinary humans (or near enough), others are\u2026 less so. The God of the Bloody Tongue, the other face of the Bloated Woman, the Haunter of the Dark. Now, if your hypothetical ST allows non-human Covers you could have some fun here. The Bloated Woman could be a fomosae, and intelligent cryptids might have handed over their souls to provide weird forms like the Haunter\u2026<br /> <br /> But there\u2019s an easier solution. The<b> Ephemeral Cover</b> Exploit. Rules are pretty sparse, but you can easily craft some horrifying spirit/ghost-forms that suit a lot of your options with it. Criminally underused, that Exploit, probably because it\u2019s a <i>lot</i> of work for player and ST.<br /> <br /> For fun, I\u2019ll probably have a crack at a Cipher that helps out even more (as it stands he can't be in lots of places at once very effectively so I'd make that the focus), but frankly I\u2019m not sure you need it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 07-26-2015, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T08:47:05-07:00","id":603852,"title":"","content":"...That's all f*cking ingenious. O.O","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T10:09:02-07:00","id":603915,"title":"","content":"Ah, to Azatoth's Court with you, Eremite! I hate it when people beat me to the punch in stuff like this.<br /> <br /> With that joke out of the way, I would like to add my observations as well. Nyarly first showed up in the story of the same name, where he awes and terrifies people with displays of scientific devices beyond the ken of that era's men. And he was mostly just mixing metal and glass. Imagine what he would have to and <i>could</i> create to awe people in the 21st century. Maybe he has an unique Merit that allows him to create 2 Gadgets per Dot of Willpower sacrificed, and a lot of dots in the <b>Suborned Infrastructure </b>Merit to help with the building of Lambda Gadgets and Precision-Engineered Gadgets. I have no doubts that he might build a Lambda Gadget with his entire Cipher inside if needed. Whatever his Cipher is.<br /> <br /> He could also have another unique Merit that gives him more leeway and speed when shaping his <b>Ephemeral Covers</b>.<br /> <br /> Also, in Dream Quest Of Unknown Kadath, Randolph Carter encounters Nyarly in the Dreamlands. So Nyarly probably has the <b>Rip The Gates</b> Exploit in order to enter the Astral Realms and other alternate dimensions. Nyarly could certainly benefit from the long distance teleportation across mundane space granted by the <b>Behind The Curtain</b> Exploit.<br /> <br /> I'll see if I can make a Cipher for him. I agree that he doesn't need to be in every single Cult and Agenda meeting simultaneously. Perhaps his Cipher has <b>Sum Of All Fears</b> as a Key somewhere, allowing Nyarly to turn into the ultimate sanity-destroying mindfuck?<br /> <br /> EDIT: by the way, I can see him as a Messenger. It is said that he enjoys causing madness a lot more than large scale destruction. That makes me think his Agendas are Tempter/Inquisitor. Tempter comes first, since he hoards secrets of every sort and stripe to make his pastime of breaking people's minds more interesting.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: it is also said that wild beasts follow him and lick his hand. If that is not just a rumor, he also has the <b>Animal Communication</b> and <b>Animal Messenger</b> Vocal Embeds. Some say he will destroy the Earth, or has already set this destruction in motion by teaching us how to build nuclear bombs, so the <b>Muse</b> Vocal Embed might fit. I also think I have the likely order of his Keys figured out:<br /> <br /> <b>Everybody Knows</b>, to start a rumor. <b>Social Engineering</b> to further move the chess pieces from the shadows. <b>Sum Of All Fears</b> to extract and process the data gained through propaganda. <b>Recurring Hallucinations</b> to make the web of lies take on a life of its own, so vivid that people go through day after day as if watched by an omnipresent, unknowable controller. In addition, he might have the <b>Urban Legend</b> and <b>Visions Of Heaven And Hell</b> Exploits to induce mass insanity when the Cipher is not suitable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-26-2015, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T12:20:27-07:00","id":603999,"title":"","content":"Nyarly certainly needs both Rip the Gates and Behind the Curtain, though frankly he'd probably have about half of the Embeds and Exploits to be appropriately powerful.<br /> <br /> Here's a quick and dirty Cipher for you, minus final secret (because some things man wasn't supposed to know). Dreams aren't always the Crawling Chaos' schtick, but some sources have some masks doing something similar and, well, it's thematically appropriate. Gotta agree with GottaGoFeast - this Cipher needed a sanity shattering power. <div align=\"center\"><b>A Thousand Masks</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Crawling Chaos has many faces, and is not bound to only appear in one place at once. By not manifesting its true power through any of its Covers, Nyarlathotep\u2019s masks can act independently. Attacking one of its masks tends to draw its full, terrible attention<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Alibi</i> and <i>Persistent Legend</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice pool:</b> Presence + Subterfuge<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Crawling Chaos\u2019s attempt to split its Covers apart draws the attention of the God-Machine. Take the Flagged Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> No effect. The demon may try again (suffering a cumulative -1 for each new attempt).<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> Nyarlathotep may manifest one of its Cover as separate entities. They can interact as normal. If the Crawling Chaos manifests Demonic Form abilities or any of its Covers switch into demonic form the waveform collapses and all the Covers fold back into the demon. By spending a point of Aether, another Cover can be manifested (no upper limit).<br /> These masks are advised to stay apart \u2013 in one another\u2019s presence each exhibits glitches.<br /> Any damage to the Cover rating of any mask ends this power \u2013 that mask is considered Nyarlathotep\u2019s true body, all other masks collapsing into it. The Wave Function Collapse Embed automatically deactivates this power in addition to any other effects, again collapsing all masks into the targeted body.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> All Aether costs are waived. <div align=\"center\"><b>Dreams Of What Is To Come</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sometimes, Nyarlathotep leaves its victims with dreams of the nightmare future that is to come. These visions gradually erode their sanity and open them to the Crawling Chaos\u2019 manipulation.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Persistent Legend </i>and <i>Recurring Hallucinations</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice pool:</b> Manipulation + Persuasion - Composure<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The target\u2019s dreams are protected, somehow, perhaps due to their strong will or some strange benefactor. They are immune to this Interlock for a lunar month.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> No effect. The demon may try again (suffering a cumulative -1 for each new attempt).<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The power affects targets for a number of days equal to Crawling Chaos\u2019 Primum. The target no longer recovers Willpower when sleeping. The glimpses of madness each night cause a Breaking Point penalised by the number of successes on the demon\u2019s activation roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The target\u2019s will is bent to serve Nyarlathotep. The demon may impose the Obsession Condition on the target, setting whatever vile task it wishes as their Obsession. They must spend a point of Willpower each scene to resist their alien compulsions. <div align=\"center\"><b>Behind The Mask</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Crawling Chaos is merely the herald of incomprehensible forces. A glimpse of its true nature can shred a person\u2019s sanity. Simply looking upon any of its masks can, if Nyarlathotep wishes, shatter a mind.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Recurring Hallucinations</i> and <i>Sum of all Fears</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice pool:</b> Presence + Intimidation - Composure<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Crawling Chaos creates an imperfect vision of horror that only strengthens its target\u2019s will. They receive the Steadfast Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> No effect. The demon may try again (suffering a cumulative -1 for each new attempt).<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The target takes the Broken Condition and rolls for a Breaking Point penalised by the number of successes on the demon\u2019s activation roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> In addition to the above, the target takes the Madness Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T12:54:59-07:00","id":604033,"title":"","content":"Oh, for the love of Yog-Sothoth. Seconds after I make the second edit to my post suggesting a Cipher! What are you, a ninja wizard?<br /> <br /> Your Cipher is awesome, by the way. Have a Like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T13:07:48-07:00","id":604041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/603759-nyarlathotep-as-a-demon?p=604033#post604033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, for the love of Yog-Sothoth. Seconds after I make the second edit to my post suggesting a Cipher! What are you, a ninja wizard?<br /> <br /> Your Cipher is awesome, by the way. Have a Like.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Something like that. Apologies for thunder-stealing, feel free to come up with your own!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T13:17:43-07:00","id":604048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/603759-nyarlathotep-as-a-demon?p=604041#post604041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Something like that. Apologies for thunder-stealing, feel free to come up with your own!</div> </div> </div> </div> To be frank, I think my Cipher would be redundant. Nyarly probably moves the chess pieces through natural talent, Cults and the like for the most part. Use of Embeds and Exploits would be minimal, and not just for secrecy. A Chess Master Cipher would be a waste when it can be a Sanity Go Squish Cipher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T15:10:32-07:00","id":604206,"title":"","content":"I decided to give Nyarly full stats. I know, true Lovecraftian horrors have no stats, but please bear with me. This was fun to to write, and if the stats sound exaggerated...you have a point, but it's friggin' <i>Nyarlathotep</i>, man. And yes, I gave him the second Process at Primum 9 instead of 10. His Demonic Form looks like a biomechanical pharaoh/shifting mass of faces, of course<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Cunning<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Sadistic/Manipulative<br /> <b>Concept:</b> Conspiracy Theorists\u2019 Worst Nightmare<br /> <br /> <b>Incarnation: </b>Messenger<br /> <b>Agenda:</b> Tempter/Inquisitor<br /> <b>Catalyst:</b> Causality<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 8, Wits 6, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 6, Manipulation 5, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Psychology) 4, Crafts (Machines) 4, Computer 4, Medicine 2, Occult 6, Politics (Secret Societies) 4, Investigation 4, Science 6<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl (No Mercy At All) 4, Drive 1, Firearms 1, Larceny 3, Stealth (Plain Sight) 3, Survival 1, Weaponry 1<br /> <br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Empathy (Body Language) 2, Expression (Speeches) 3, Intimidation (Sudden Seriousness) 4, Persuasion 5, Socialize 1, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge (Propaganda) 5<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Psychology, Machines, Speeches), Common Sense, Encyclopedic Knowlegde (Crafts, Science, Occult), Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Epic</b></a>), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Psychology), Patient, Professional Training 5 (Crafts, Science, Occult), Tolerance For Biology, Trained Observer 1, Vice-Ridden, Ambidextrous, Iron Stamina 3, Sleight Of Hand, Allies (Anything Needed), Closed Book 4, Contacts (Anything Needed), Fixer, Inspiring, Iron Will, Resources 5, Pusher, Status (Anything Needed), Striking Looks 2 (Sinister), Table Turner, Untouchable, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Light Weapons 4 (Natural Weaponry), Advanced Form, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794814#post794814\"><b>Advanced Self-Repair System 5</b></a>, Bolthole (Anything Needed), Consummate Professional (Tempter, Inquisitor), Cultists 5, Efficient Dealer, Electromagnetic Linguistics, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=1022283#post1022283\"><b>Ephemeral Integration</b></a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=847701#post847701\"><b>Evolved Form 4</b></a> (Claws And Fangs, Glory And Terror, Teleportation, Amorphous), Living The Lie, Monkeywrencher, Multiple Agendas, Resonance Sensitivity, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=932094#post932094\"><b>Suborned Facility</b></a> (Anything Needed), Subborned Infrastructure 3, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=847701#post847701\"><b>Supernatural Integration 5</b></a>, Terrible Form 4, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=848219#post848219\"><b>Transcend Incarnation (Analyst)</b></a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=956486#post956486\"><b>Supernatural Infiltration</b></a>, Versatile Transformation<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Embeds</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Vocal:</b> All of them, maybe take out one or two<br /> <br /> <b>Instrumental:</b> Efficiency, Ellipses, Fungible Knowledge, High Of Birth, Open Sesame, Read Hostility, Wasted Time<br /> <br /> <b>Cacophony:</b> Cause And Effect, Cool Heads Prevail, Devil\u2019s Advocate, Lucky Break, Just Bruised, On The Mend, Shatter, Shifty Eyes, Special Someone, Tag &amp; Release<br /> <br /> <b>Mundane:</b> Alibi, Associate And Integrate, Authorized, Deep Cover, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=855075#post855075\"><b>Face Off</b></a>, Going Native, Idle Conversation, In My Pocket, Identity Theft, Lost In The Crowd, Never Here, Persistent Legend, Quick Change, Without A Trace, You Can Tell Me<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Exploits</b></span><br /> <br /> Behind The Curtain, Context Matters, Decoy, Deep Pockets, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=839313#post839313\"><b>Demonic Might</b></a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=855075#post855075\"><b>Form Of The Beast</b></a>, Ephemeral Cover, Living Shadow, Rip The Gates, Sermon, Show Of Power, Swarm, Terrible Avatar, Two Places At Once, Urban Legend, Visions Of Heaven And Hell<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Demonic Form</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Modifications:</b> Claws And Fangs, Huge Size, Armored Plates, Tough As Stone<br /> <br /> <b>Technologies:</b> Aura Sight, Clairvoyant Sight, Glory And Terror, Mind Reading<br /> <br /> <b>Propulsions:</b> Phasing, Teleportation<br /> <br /> <b>Processes:</b> Dataform, Amorphous, Nanobot Composition, Multiple Images<br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <b>Primum:</b> 9<br /> <b>Cover:</b> 8","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-26-2016, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T18:27:58-07:00","id":604372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/603759-nyarlathotep-as-a-demon?p=604206#post604206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Merits: </b>Vice-Ridden, Ambidextrous, Area Of Expertise (Machines, Secret Societies), Quick Draw, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Anything Needed), Common Sense, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Striking Looks +2 (Creepy), Inspiring, <b>Well-Traveled</b>, Allies/Contacts (Anything Needed), Resources X (Anything Needed), <b>Living The Lie</b>, Resonance Sensitive, Resonance Aware, Versatile Transformation, Multiple Agendas, Consummate Professional (Tempter, Inquisitor), <b>Electromagnetic Linguistics</b>, <b>Monkeywrencher</b>, Bolthole X (Anything Needed), Cultists X (Anything Needed), Suborned Infrastructure X (Anything Needed), Gadget Wizard (2 Gadgets per Willpower Dot), Terrible Form 4</div> </div> </div> </div>Curious, what are those particular merits that I've bolded? I figure they're probably specific in some way to Mummy perhaps, but I'm not familiar with them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T18:48:57-07:00","id":604386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/603759-nyarlathotep-as-a-demon?p=604372#post604372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Curious, what are those particular merits that I've bolded? I figure they're probably specific in some way to Mummy perhaps, but I'm not familiar with them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well-Traveled (Reliquary, page 85): 9 Again on Mental and Social rolls regarding customs of foreign cultures.<br /> <br /> Living The Lie: When you acquire a new Cover, choose a Virtue and Vice for that identity. While you're using that Cover, you can regain Willpower by channeling either your own Virtue and Vice or the Cover's.<br /> <br /> Electromagnetic Linguistics: You are more in tune with the &quot;machine&quot; portion of the God-Machine than most. In addition to all native human languages, you can decipher machine code, programming languages, and even electromagnetic signals. This can range from reading a piece of computer code and instinctively understanding what the program is intended to do to &quot;hearing&quot; text messages as they zip through the air. Wireless broadcasts can be plucked from the air, but information sent via landline requires you to physically plug a cable into your body. (This doesn't inflict any damage, but it's disconcerting and counts as a compromise if you're under Cover.) Encrypted data isn't automatically deciphered, but you can try to hack it just like if you had the data on a computer. In especially signal-dense areas, like major first-world cities where lots of people have smartphones and wi-fi networks and such, the Storyteller might call for a Wits + Composure roll to isolate a particular transmission, much like trying to listen to a single conversation in a crowded room.<br /> <br /> Monkeywrencher: Your character has a strong affinity for the nature of her Embeds. Because of this, your character can negate Embeds that match her Incarnation, or her Cipher. When another demon uses an Embed that fits either your character's Incarnation or a known Key, she can reflexively attempt to counter it by temporarily negating the logistical loophole in reality that allows the Embed to engage. She can also attempt to Monkeywrench any time an angel activates a Numen. Spend an Aether and roll Resolve + Primum. Successes subtract from the user's activation roll. Drawback: Use of Monkeywrencher is always a compromise. The first time in a scene, the compromise is made at +1. Each time thereafter, it's made at a cumulative -1.<br /> <br /> The last 3 are from &quot;Flowers Of Hell: The Demon Player's Guide&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T19:00:11-07:00","id":604387,"title":"","content":"Well, I feel silly now.<br /> <br /> I recently re-read the Player's Guide and I've completely missed those Merits. Thanks for the reliquary one though, I don't have that book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T19:09:43-07:00","id":604394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/603759-nyarlathotep-as-a-demon?p=604387#post604387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I feel silly now.<br /> <br /> I recently re-read the Player's Guide and I've completely missed those Merits. Thanks for the reliquary one though, I don't have that book.</div> </div> </div> </div> You can always check out the <a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WoD Canon Index</a> and the <a href=\"http://rp.thesubnet.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Subnet</a>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}